          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "lēx, lēgis — \"a law\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Populus novam lēgem probāvit. The people approved the new law."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine, 3rd declension. A lēx was a bill passed by the people's vote. English legal comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "lēx is inherited from Proto-Italic lēg- (EtymDB); Lewis & Short connect it, with doubt, with a root meaning \"to bind\". English legal and legislate come from it."
            }
          ]
        },
